  "question": "A rental company has multiple branches, with branch information including name, address, and manager name. Each branch manages a certain number of vehicles. Vehicles have license plate numbers, models, year, and rental rates. Customer information includes name, phone number, and email. Customers can rent vehicles, with each rental recording rental time, return time, and rental fee. The rental company needs to record the income of each branch for performance evaluation.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0212\n\nCREATE TABLE `branch` (\n  `branch_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `branch_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `manager_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`branch_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `vehicle` (\n  `vehicle_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `branch_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `license_plate` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `model` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `year` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `rental_rate` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`vehicle_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `vehicle_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`branch_id`) REFERENCES `branch` (`branch_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `customer` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `customer_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `rental` (\n  `rental_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `vehicle_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `branch_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `rental_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `return_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `rental_fee` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`rental_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `rental_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `rental_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`vehicle_id`) REFERENCES `vehicle` (`vehicle_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `rental_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`branch_id`) REFERENCES `branch` (`branch_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `branch_income` (\n  `income_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `branch_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `record_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `total_income` decimal(12,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`income_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `branch_income_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`branch_id`) REFERENCES `branch` (`branch_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
